  "Id": 426,
  "Title": "Dr Mir Afzal Tajik participates in a Comparative, International and Development Education Centre Seminar 2013",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "Dr Mir Afzal Tajik, Assistant Professor and Head of Graduate Programmes, AKU-IED, was invited as a guest speaker by the Comparative, International and Development Education Centre (CIDEC) of the Ontario Institute for Studies in Education, University",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<div class=\"ExternalClassFEF896B01E174426AF8AA87EB70B1DD7\"><p>Dr Mir Afzal Tajik, Assistant Professor and Head of Graduate Programmes, AKU-IED, was invited as a guest speaker by the Comparative, International and Development Education Centre (CIDEC) of the Ontario Institute for Studies in Education, University of Toronto, Canada, to give a talk on \"Transforming Teaching Practice in Afghanistan\" in CIDEC Seminar on February 20, 2013. Dr Tajik delivered his address through video conference to the CIDEC Seminar. The seminar participants represented faculty, students and researchers of OISE/UT. The talk was very well received by the audience.</p></div>",
